#!grafli v1
# Order Processing sub-grafli
# This file demonstrates when to split a complex node into its own diagram.

@ note title 40,20 "Order Processing detail" ~xlarge
@ note hint 40,80 "Parent graph stays high-level; this sub-grafli expands the order lifecycle." ~small

@ box receive "Receive request" 60,160 180x80 %primary
@ box reserve "Reserve inventory" 320,160 200x80 %secondary
@ box authorize "Authorize payment" 600,160 200x80 %secondary
@ box persist "Persist order" 880,160 180x80 %tertiary
@ box publish "Publish event" 1140,160 180x80 %accent

@ arrow receive -> reserve "step: 1"
@ arrow reserve -> authorize "step: 2"
@ arrow authorize -> persist "step: 3"
@ arrow persist -> publish "event: OrderCreated"

@ note flow_code 320,300 """
code:
fn: completeOrder(req) -> OrderId
pre: inventory reservation exists
call: payment.authorize(req.total)
set: order.status = confirmed
emit: OrderCreated(order.id)
post: reservation consumed exactly once
verify: trace stops when event is observed
""" ~small !mono

@ note review 880,320 "Q: Should payment timeout publish a compensating ReservationReleased event?" ~small
